  "problem": "Which of the following diagrams shows all the $3$rd roots of unity?",
  "worked_solution": "Geometrically, the $3$rd roots of unity have the following properties:\n\n- all of them lie on the unit circle centered in the origin,\n\n- one of the roots is $1,$ corresponding to the point $(1,0)$ on the complex plane,\n\n- the roots form an equilateral triangle (regular $3$-sided polygon).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995561/assets/c70d25ac3a5ddb2d6765ef8a22f5e9774c9be06dd909d7079c3a361157881bb5.png)",
